[[File:Radermachera sinica.jpg|thumb|''[[Radermachera sinica]]'' as a houseplant]]
'''''Radermachera''''' is a [[genus]] of about 17 [[species]] of [[flowering plant]]s in the family [[Bignoniaceae]], native to southeastern [[Asia]]. They are [[evergreen]] [[tree]]s reaching 5–40 m tall, with bipinnate to tripinnate [[leaf|leaves]], and panicles of large bell-shaped, white, pink, pale purple or yellow [[flower]]s 5–7&nbsp;cm diameter.

The genus is named after [[Jacob Cornelis Matthieu Radermacher]], the 18th century Dutch naturalist who cataloged much of the flora of Java and Sumatra.

